---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PhotoBlock from '../components/PhotoBlock.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Ayara Foundation: the story behind our name, our mission and how we work with local partners across Sierra Leone, Zimbabwe, The Gambia and Kenya."
>
  <section class="section intro-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal"><a href="/">&larr; Home</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">About Ayara</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        We support practical skills, self-reliance and community-led
        action for people, livelihoods and nature.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section name-section">
    <div class="wrap name-grid">
      <h2 class="reveal">Where the Name Comes From</h2>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          The name Ayara is inspired by Ay&eacute;, which refers to the
          physical world, and Ara, meaning mystery or wonder, in Yoruba.
          For us, Ayara stands for a world that is understood, cared for
          and shaped together.
        </p>
        <p>
          At the heart of Ayara is the relationship between people and
          nature. Healthy livelihoods depend on land, water, soil,
          forests, materials, skills and local ecosystems. We support
          projects that bring these dimensions together, creating income
          and opportunity while protecting, restoring and responsibly
          using the natural environment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PhotoBlock src="/images/focus-nature.jpg" alt="Aerial view of natural landscape" tone="forest" reverse>
    <h2 class="reveal">Ideas Into Fundable Projects</h2>
    <p class="reveal">
      Our work focuses on projects that strengthen local knowledge,
      hands-on learning, women&rsquo;s and youth opportunities, shared
      community infrastructure and care for the natural environment. We
      work with local partners to turn practical ideas into fundable
      projects that communities can use, own and grow.
    </p>
  </PhotoBlock>

  <section class="section what-section">
    <div class="wrap what-grid">
      <h2 class="reveal">What This Looks Like in Practice</h2>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          Ayara&rsquo;s current portfolio spans vocational training,
          community workshops, access to tools, sustainable building,
          circular economy enterprises, agro-processing and women-led
          livelihood initiatives, each one shaped by the specific local
          needs it responds to.
        </p>
        <p>
          Projects currently run in Sierra Leone, Zimbabwe, The Gambia,
          Nigeria and Kenya, each shaped with a local partner who leads
          implementation on the ground. Ayara&rsquo;s role is to help
          turn a workable local idea into a project that funders can
          back and communities can sustain.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every project carries a monitoring, evaluation, accountability
          and learning (MEAL) component, so results are tracked
          honestly and lessons feed back into how the next project is
          designed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="wrap cta-inner reveal">
      <h2>See What We&rsquo;re Working On</h2>
      <p>Explore our focus areas or get in touch about a partnership.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="/focus">Our Focus Areas</a>
        <a class="pill-btn outline" href="/contact">Contact Us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 640px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .name-section {
    background: var(--sky-soft);
  }

  .name-grid,
  .what-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.6fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
  }

  .cta {
    background: var(--sun-pale);
  }

  .cta-inner {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .cta-inner p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .name-grid,
    .what-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
